  "body_markdown": "Skip to content\n\nDental Implants\n\nDental Implant Surgery\n\nAll-on-4 Dental Implants\n\nFixed Teeth vs. Removable\n\nCost & Compare\n\nDental Implant FAQ\n\nAesthetics\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nPorcelain Veneers\n\nDental Crowns & Bridges\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nTreatments\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nOral Surgery\n\nEmergency Dentistry\n\nConditions We Treat\n\nWhat To Expect\n\nPatient Center\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nSmile Gallery\n\nWho We Are\n\nWhy Choose Us\n\nMeet Dr. Esam Nahlah\n\nMeet The Team\n\nVideo Library\n\nPatient Stories\n\nFor Doctors\n\nReferral Form\n\nContact Us\n\nBlog\n\nCurrent Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria: (703) 940-5410\n\nNew Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (571) 619-9442\n\nAlexandria: (571) 410-3430\n\nBook now\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## Porcelain Veneers – The Answers to Your Questions\n\n\nJune 15, 2022\n\n\n#### Share This Post\n\n\nIf you have questions about Porcelain Veneers, this post is for you. We answer the most common questions about it.\n\n\n## What Are Porcelain Veneers?\n\n\nVery different than Dental Implants, the veneers are a very thin layer of porcelain that bonds to the teeth surface, they help change the color and the shape of the teeth permanently, so if the patient has worn-down teeth, which can happen by age or any other condition, like grinding teeth (bruxism) or tetracycline staining, we can get the patient back to a healthy, normal, and beautiful smile, with a permanent bright smile.\n\n\n## What is the difference between Veneers and Crowns?\n\n\nVeneers are very thin layers of porcelain, about 0.5 mm bonded on the outside surfaces of the teeth, they can change the color and the shape of the tooth. These are a much more conservative treatment and preserve the natural structure of the teeth.\n\nCrowns require shaving the whole teeth all-around 360 degrees which leads to much more loss of the natural teeth structure and more invasive preparations of the teeth which can lead to the need for root canal therapy the teeth or extreme sensitivity of the teeth.\n\nBefore Dr. Nahlah Patient Photo\n\nAfter Dr. Nahlah Patient Photo\n\n\n## Do Veneers Ruin your teeth?\n\n\nVeneers do not ruin the teeth if they are done correctly.\n\n\n## Is permanent?\n\n\nYes. Porcelain Veneers are permanent, they do not change colors over time.\n\n\n## What are the process?\n\n\nIn our practice Dr. Nahlah performs Veneers in 3 visits, these visits are done in 3 weeks.\n\nThe first visit is the smile design, during this visit Dr. Nahlah and his in-house lab designer meet with the patient and design the future smile of the patient as well taking initial records of photographs of the face and smile of the patient. Dr. Nahlah will spend many hours with his lab designer in his in-house state-of-the-art digital lab to craft a personal smile for each patient. Once this design is ready, the patient will be scheduled for the second visit, during that visit Dr. Nahlah will perform a mock-up of the designed smile and show it to the patient before performing the veneers, so the patient has the chance to review their smile before the procedure is done, at this stage any alteration of the design can be performed easily and retry in the patient mouth until the patient is completely happy and satisfied with the design, then Dr. Nahlah will prep the teeth, take a final scan (digital impression ) and put temporary veneers that will be a copy of the final design.\n\nThe patient will wear these temporary veneers until the final are ready.\n\nFinal porcelain veneers will be made in our in-house state-of-the-art lab so we have the full capacity of crafting beautiful veneers with high-quality porcelain and an amazing look.\n\nIn the third visit, Dr. Nahlah will remove the temporary and bond the final permanently.\n\n\n### Schedule a Free Consultation\n\n\nDo you feel like this is the best solution for your smile?\n\nFill out the form below and our treatment coordinator will reach out to you briefly.\n\n[contact-form-7 id=”6391″ title=”Lead Form Home”]\n\nPrevPreviousDental Implants – Everything You Need to Know\n\nNextAre There Factors That Determine Which Type Of Dental Implant Procedure I Can Get Treated With?Next\n\n\n#### More To Explore\n\n\n\n### Unlock the Benefits of Dental Implants: Your Best Teeth Replacement Option\n\n\nTooth loss can become an unfortunate reality for many as we age. Thankfully, advancements in dental technology, like dental implants,\n\nRead More »\n\nOctober 26, 2024\n\n\n### Your Comprehensive Guide on Dental Implants: The Best Replacement of Tooth Solution\n\n\nDental implants in McLean, VA are small, and titanium posts are surgically placed in your jawbone underneath your gum line.\n\nOctober 20, 2024\n\n\n## You Are Welcome Here.\n\n\nSchedule your consultation today.\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddresses:\n\nTysons Corner\n\n7901 Jones Branch Dr., Suite 220\n\nMcLean, VA 22102\n\nNew Patients: (571) 619-9442\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria\n\n2855 Duke St,\n\nAlexandria, VA 22314\n\nNew Patients: (571) 410-3430\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 940-5410\n\n\n#### Hours\n\n\nMonday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nTuesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nWednesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nThursday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nFriday: 8:00am – 2:00pm\n\nSaturday: Closed\n\nSunday: Closed\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\nAll-On-4® Implants\n\nCrowns & Bridges\n\n\n#### About Us\n\n\nMeet the Doctor\n\nAbout Us\n\nBefore & After Photos\n\n2025 Dr. Nahlah. All rights reserved",
